  "sent_to_model": "I need a one-page announcement for our first Fix-It Saturday at St. Ansgar. It goes up on the church website and gets printed for the coffee shops and the library branch on Minnehaha, so it's for the whole neighborhood, not just members. Council finally approved it last week and I confess I'm thrilled about it. Dates, times and the list of fixers are below. Please include the practical details and volunteer request below.\n\n- first Fix-It Saturday is Dec 5, 2026, 9 a.m. to 1 p.m., Fellowship Hall, St. Ansgar Lutheran Church, Minneapolis, MN, enter by the alley door (ramp)\n- free, no membership, no sign-up; donations to the food shelf welcome but not expected\n- volunteer fixers so far - small appliances, lamps, bikes, clothing mending, knife sharpening, one retired tech guy for laptops and phones\n- one item per person to start, so the line moves; coffee and kringle provided\n- after that, first Saturday of every month through spring\n- Doris Lindqvist, 84, has darned socks for this parish since the Carter years and asked to run the mending table herself\n- Marv Okafor fixed my 1970s Hamilton Beach mixer in twenty minutes in the church kitchen; that's when the idea was born\n- too much gets thrown away that just needs a screw or a new cord\n- this is good neighboring, plain and simple; no strings, nobody will preach at you\n- people should bring the broken toaster AND stay for coffee\n- ask for more volunteer fixers, especially anyone who can do vacuums or zippers\n- contact the church office, office@stansgarlutheran.example or 612-555-0148\n\n(About me: Lutheran pastor, 61, Minneapolis, Minnesota. Length: it should come to roughly 250-400 words.)",
